ng soda keg compresses the soda further, making it so dangerous that it was banned by the ATAO just three days after release. It packs an even bigger punch.\nPerhaps a skull with a hole in it will one day be displayed in the Columbian Aerospace Museum, commemorating the wrong turns in the development of flight technology.","abilities":["Flying unit.","Gradually accelerates when moving, but loses HP over time; the first attack after being blocked deals bonus damage based on Movement Speed, and blows away Balloons and Powerful Balloons at the target's tile"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.3,"stats":{"hp":13000,"atk":650,"def":400,"res":10,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":3.5}},"skystrider_ambulance":{"slug":"skystrider_ambulance","name":"Skystrider Ambulance","icon":"/enemies-icons/Skystrider Ambulance.webp","rank":"Elite","race":"Drone","movement":"Flying","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Learning from their previous mistakes, Volvort Kochinski R&D repurposed the failed flying restroom into an ambulance.\nUnfortunately, their invention was still ahead of its time. Not everywhere in Propeller Paradise has a landing pad, and grabbing patients with pincers was considered too rough.","abilities":["Flying unit.","When defeated for the first time, crashes and becomes debris with extremely high DEF, nullifying 1 Buoyancy if on a Levitatable Zone"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.3,"stats":{"hp":18000,"atk":900,"def":1200,"res":0,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":4}},"sunchaser_tree":{"slug":"sunchaser_tree","name":"'Sunchaser Tree'","icon":"/enemies-icons/'Sunchaser Tree'.webp","rank":"Elite","race":"Drone","movement":"Flying","attackPosition":"Ranged","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"In the era of Sky Fever, everything must fly, even trees. What once planted its roots in the soil now flies away to every corner of Terra.\nThey chase the sun according to their primal instincts, and even their leaves have been dyed red.","abilities":["Flying unit.","Only attacks allied units in aerial state"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.4,"stats":{"hp":50000,"atk":3000,"def":600,"res":30,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":5.5}},"v_la_of_convallis":{"slug":"v_la_of_convallis","name":"Væla of Convallis","icon":"/enemies-icons/Væla of Convallis.webp","rank":"Boss","race":"Sarkaz","movement":"Flying","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical","Arts"],"flavourText":"If only there were something she could still do, for Convallis, for the Banshee, for her.","abilities":["Attacks deal Physical damage and splash damage to allied units, Balloons, and Powerful Balloons in a large area around the target","[Return to Oblivion] Sequentially locks on to up to 2 allied units, dealing gradually increasing Arts damage; if the unit retreats or is defeated, nullifies 2 additional Buoyancy on their Levitatable Zone for the remainder of the skill; prioritizes low ground units","ATK, DEF, and RES reduced for a period of time when [Return to Oblivion] expires; the more targets the skill had, the longer the duration","When HP drops to 0 for the first time, takes the battlefield into the sky and revives","Flight Phase","Permanent Field Change: All units on the ground are defeated, and tiles and Levitatable Zones on the ground are destroyed","Increases starting ATK, DEF, and RES; immune to Stun, Freeze, and Fear; [Return to Oblivion] locks onto 1 additional target"],"levelCount":2,"level":1,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.5,"stats":{"hp":110000,"atk":1700,"def":2400,"res":50,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":6}}},"dropIcons":{"4002":"/item-icons/originite_prime.png"},"previewFile":"ur-ex-8.webp","emergency":null,"devices":[],"playbackPaths":{"0":{"points":[[